$VER: GetRecent V1.2a (17-9-1996)
      Freely redistributable Version

      Program by Massimiliano Pala (m.pala@mo.nettuno.it)


DESCRIPTION

	I  wrote  this software mainly because I needed a way to Download Safetly
and  automatically  from the Internet the New Files found on Aminet.  Here it
comes  GetRecent:   it  will  automatically download from aminet the software
listed  in  a  RECENT  file (either local or over the net) to the appropriate
directory setting in the Comment field of the file its brief description.


INSTALLATION

	GetRecent  simply uses the FTP:  device to access files over the net.  If
you  have  already installed FTPMount then you quite surely have configured a
directory  to  access  the aminet archive nearer to you ( faster...  ), let's
assume  this  directory  is  FTP:aminet (please make sure to be in the aminet
directory,  i.e.   add  a Tooltype in the aminet icon ROOT=pub/aminet or what
the main aminet directory is).

	Ok, now simply copy the Main file to some directory in your Path, I moved
it  on  AmiTCP:bin/.  Ok...  the installation is complete.  Let's look at the
arguments...


USAGE

	Following a full list of the arguments used:

GETDIR=DDIR/A :  (Needed) This is the LOCAL main directory of the aminet dir,
	in  this  path  there  should  be all the directories and sub directories
	found on the AMINET ( comm, biz, demo, game, ecc...  )


AMINETDIR=ADIR/A  :   (Needed)  This  is the NET main dir.  As explained this
	program  needs  FTPMount  in  order  to  work,  so this is usually set to
	FTP:aminet


DENYDIRS=DENY/S/K :  This is a Boolean value.  Specifying this word, will be
	discaded  files in the dirs :  mods, pix, demo.  I usually do not need to
	waste money for this bits... if you do, do not use this word.


RECENT=RECENTFILE/K  :   The  Program  will  (if not already present in DDIR)
	download the RECENT file from Aminet.  If you want to use a local file as
	the  files holding the software to be downloaded, use this command ( i.e.
	if  you  want to download some specific software prepare the file offline
	and launch the program when online ).


MAXDIM/N/K  :  This is the maximum lenght of files specified in Kbytes.  File
	bigger then this value will not be downloaded.


MAXSECS/N/K :  Maximum time to be spent online.  Usefull if you want to run
	in batch mode in the late hours of the day when phone lines are cheeper
	and you do not have to stay in fron of your computer all the time...


LOGFILE=LOG/K :  The name of the Log file.  Possible use is to prepare a list
	of new files arrived at your host (bbs ???).


HEADER/K  :   Header  file.   The  contents  of  this file will be put at the
	beginning of the log file.


FOOTER/K :  Mostly like the Header, except the contents of this file will be
	appended to the log.


PUBSCREEN=PUBS/K  :   Use  this  option  if you want the program to open it's
	window on a specific pubblic screen. Default is Workbench.


COMMENTS

	This  is  the  Second  Release of the Archive, I found a Bug on the First
Release  of  the  Software  that caused a wrong SetCommand() option.  Perhaps
there  will  be  other  new  releases  wich  will  improve the File-Selection
Cacapibilities...  So Stay Tuned!!!

	I made a 1.2+ O.S.  Compatible version for the ones that have not updated
their hardware ( what are you waiting for ??  ), if you need I can Re-Compile
the source for your needs ( CPU, OS, etcc... ).

	Do  you  think a MUI version have to be released ??  Please report me any
bug, comment or suggestion you can think of.  Please, E-Mail me if you use it
because...  I like it!  :-))

	Last  but  not  Least :  thank you for your comment and suggetions!  This
little program found a quite big success among the Amiga community...  please
support me with your E-Mail!

	Good Download with GetRecent, and long life to Aminet and Amiga!



